Z||000005||William||05-03-2000||12:53 AM||||My dash has a defect, but not where most of the dashes break. My ac vent bottoms are mint, however there is a small place on top of my dash (at the edge of the defroster vent) where the vinyl is starting to rise up and become kinda of wavy. Anyone else having this problem? Since even a good dash from the yards will still be 15 years old and prone to cracking, I thought about having the top of the dash recovered in leather by a shop, or even try to do it myself with leather or the fake leather stuff. There is an indentation separating the top of the dash from the bottom and would be a good place to make the transition. Any thought here guys?||||reg||5
